  "summary": "`Seekable` reads a NULL or out-of-bounds seek table",
  "details": "`Seekable` did not record whether it was initialized. On a fresh `Seekable`,\nor one whose `init_buff()` failed, `decompress`, `offset_to_frame_index` and\n`frame_decompressed_size` made the C library read a NULL seek table. After a\nfailed re-initialization, `decompress` returned data from the refused buffer\nusing the previous seek table.\n\nSeparately, `frame_decompressed_size(num_frames())`, on `Seekable` and\n`SeekTable`, read one entry past the end of the seek table.\n\nThe flaw was corrected by refusing to use a `Seekable` until an\ninitialization succeeded, and by checking the frame index.",
  "severity": [],
